# CSharpier 1.x formats XML as well as C#, so .csproj and .xml are in scope by default —
# the overrides block in .csharpierrc.yaml only tunes that, it does not enable it, and there
# is no "formatter: none" to opt a pattern out. This file is the only lever.
#
# Both are hand-managed here. The csproj Condition expressions in particular read worse
# escaped: csharpier rewrites -> as -&gt; inside the attribute.
*.csproj
*.xml
